  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.3.0 adds Hosking-Wallis regional frequency analysis (Numerics.Distributions.Regional), Gaussian process regression, kriging, elastic net and PCA, the L-BFGS-B, CMA-ES and DDS optimizers with Pareto-front, dynamic programming and knapsack utilities, a QL eigensolver, an opt-in QAGS integrator, multi-source CSR shortest paths, column statistics, compensated sums, and per-element Poisson and Binomial array members. It fixes accuracy defects in StudentT, the incomplete beta and inverse incomplete gamma functions, the Joe, Clayton, Frank and Gumbel copula densities, GEV, Gamma and Pearson Type III L-moments, variance, covariance and Pearson correlation on offset data, and Kernel Density and Truncated modes. GoodnessOfFit.KolmogorovSmirnov and AndersonDarling now sort a copy of unsorted input, with new dataIsSorted overloads. GEV ParametersFromLinearMoments now throws for a non-positive L-scale, and Dijkstra and Network reject negative edge weights. The net10.0 build is tested on Windows and Linux, and the pynumerics Python package, which ships this assembly, is published to PyPI with each release. Breaking: the package targets net10.0 and net481 only; .NET 8 and .NET 9 reach end of support on November 10, 2026, so projects on those runtimes can stay on 2.2.0. See the v2.3.0 GitHub release notes for the full list and the results that move.",
